Feature: Enrich patient_therapy_shipment with derived metrics for adherence, therapy gaps, age, and discontinuation

  Background:
    Given the source table "purgo_playground.patient_therapy_shipment" exists in Unity Catalog
    And the table contains the following columns:
      | product | ship_date | days_supply | qty | treatment_id | dob | first_ship_date | refill_status | patient_id | ship_type | shipment_arrived_status | delivery_ontime | calctime |
    And the output table "enriched_patient_therapy_shipment" is defined with all source columns plus 12 derived columns
    And the calculation logic for derived columns is as specified in logic.xlsx

  Scenario Outline: Successful enrichment of patient_therapy_shipment with derived metrics
    Given a row in patient_therapy_shipment with valid values for all required columns
    When the enrichment process runs
    Then the output row contains all source columns, with qty converted to string
    And the following derived columns are calculated:
      | shipment_expiry         | DATE_ADD(ship_date, cast(COALESCE(days_supply, qty / 3*7 ) as int)) |
      | discontinuation_date    | DATE_ADD(shipment_expiry, 91)                                       |
      | days_until_next_ship    | DATEDIFF(shipment_expiry, calctime) + 1                             |
      | days_since_last_fill    | DATEDIFF(calctime, ship_date) + 1                                   |
      | expected_refill_date    | DATE_ADD(calctime, days_until_next_ship)                            |
      | prior_ship              | LAG(ship_date) OVER(PARTITION BY treatment_id ORDER BY ship_date)   |
      | days_between            | DATEDIFF(ship_date, prior_ship)                                     |
      | days_since_supply_out   | CASE WHEN DATEDIFF(calctime, shipment_expiry) >= 0 THEN DATEDIFF(calctime, shipment_expiry) ELSE NULL |
      | age                     | FLOOR(DATEDIFF(DAY, dob, calctime) / 365.25)                        |
      | age_at_first_ship       | ROUND(DATEDIFF(DAY, dob, first_ship_date) / 365.0, 0)               |
      | latest_therapy_ships    | COUNT(ship_date) OVER(PARTITION BY patient_id, treatment_id WHERE ship_type='commercial') |
      | discontinuation_type    | CASE WHEN refill_status = 'DC - Standard' THEN 'STANDARD' WHEN refill_status = 'DC-PERMANENT' THEN 'PERMANENT' ELSE NULL |
    And the output row is displayed in enriched_patient_therapy_shipment

    Examples:
      | product | ship_date   | days_supply | qty | treatment_id | dob        | first_ship_date | refill_status     | patient_id | ship_type   | shipment_arrived_status | delivery_ontime | calctime            |
      | DrugA   | 2024-01-01  | 28          | 84  | TREAT001     | 1980-05-10 | 2024-01-01      | DC - Standard     | PAT001     | commercial  | arrived                | yes             | 2024-01-29 00:00:00 |
      | DrugB   | 2024-02-15  | NULL        | 63  | TREAT002     | 1975-12-20 | 2024-02-15      | DC-PERMANENT      | PAT002     | commercial  | arrived                | no              | 2024-03-20 00:00:00 |
      | DrugC   | 2024-03-10  | 30          | 90  | TREAT003     | 1990-07-01 | 2024-03-10      | ACTIVE            | PAT003     | commercial  | pending                | yes             | 2024-04-10 00:00:00 |
      | DrugD   | 2024-04-05  | NULL        | 21  | TREAT004     | 2000-01-01 | 2024-04-05      | DC - Standard     | PAT004     | noncommercial| arrived               | yes             | 2024-05-01 00:00:00 |
      | DrugE   | 2024-05-20  | 14          | 42  | TREAT005     | 1965-03-15 | 2024-05-20      | DC-PERMANENT      | PAT005     | commercial  | arrived                | yes             | 2024-06-10 00:00:00 |

  Scenario Outline: Validation error for missing required fields
    Given a row in patient_therapy_shipment with missing <missing_column>
    When the enrichment process runs
    Then an error is raised: "Missing required field: <missing_column>"
    And the row is not processed

    Examples:
      | missing_column         |
      | product               |
      | ship_date             |
      | treatment_id          |
      | patient_id            |
      | dob                   |
      | first_ship_date       |
      | qty                   |

  Scenario Outline: Validation error for type mismatch
    Given a row in patient_therapy_shipment where <column> has an invalid type
    When the enrichment process runs
    Then an error is raised: "Type mismatch in column: <column>"
    And the row is not processed

    Examples:
      | column      |
      | ship_date   |
      | dob         |
      | qty         |
      | days_supply |

  Scenario Outline: Handling NULL or missing days_supply and qty
    Given a row in patient_therapy_shipment where days_supply is NULL and qty is <qty>
    When the enrichment process runs
    Then shipment_expiry is calculated using qty / 3*7 if qty is not NULL
    And if both days_supply and qty are NULL, an error is raised: "Cannot calculate shipment_expiry: missing days_supply and qty"

    Examples:
      | qty  |
      | 84   |
      | NULL |

  Scenario Outline: Handling first shipment (no prior_ship)
    Given a row in patient_therapy_shipment that is the first shipment for a treatment_id
    When the enrichment process runs
    Then prior_ship is NULL
    And days_between is NULL

    Examples:
      | treatment_id | ship_date   | prior_ship |
      | TREAT001     | 2024-01-01  | NULL       |
      | TREAT002     | 2024-02-15  | NULL       |

  Scenario Outline: Discontinuation type mapping
    Given a row in patient_therapy_shipment with refill_status = <refill_status>
    When the enrichment process runs
    Then discontinuation_type is mapped as follows:
      | DC - Standard   | STANDARD   |
      | DC-PERMANENT    | PERMANENT  |
      | <other>         | NULL       |

    Examples:
      | refill_status   | expected_discontinuation_type |
      | DC - Standard   | STANDARD                     |
      | DC-PERMANENT    | PERMANENT                    |
      | ACTIVE          | NULL                         |
      | DC-OTHER        | NULL                         |

  Scenario Outline: latest_therapy_ships calculation
    Given multiple rows for the same patient_id and treatment_id with ship_type = <ship_type>
    When the enrichment process runs
    Then latest_therapy_ships is the count of ship_date for patient_id, treatment_id where ship_type = 'commercial'

    Examples:
      | patient_id | treatment_id | ship_type    | expected_count |
      | PAT001     | TREAT001     | commercial   | 3              |
      | PAT002     | TREAT002     | noncommercial| 0              |
      | PAT003     | TREAT003     | commercial   | 1              |

  Scenario Outline: qty type conversion
    Given a row in patient_therapy_shipment with qty as bigint
    When the enrichment process runs
    Then qty is converted to string in the output

    Examples:
      | qty_in_source | qty_in_output |
      | 84            | "84"          |
      | 21            | "21"          |

  Scenario Outline: Error on duplicate rows (same patient_id, treatment_id, ship_date)
    Given two rows in patient_therapy_shipment with the same patient_id, treatment_id, and ship_date
    When the enrichment process runs
    Then an error is raised: "Duplicate shipment record for patient_id, treatment_id, ship_date"
    And only one row is processed

    Examples:
      | patient_id | treatment_id | ship_date   |
      | PAT001     | TREAT001     | 2024-01-01  |
      | PAT002     | TREAT002     | 2024-02-15  |

  Scenario Outline: Error on invalid date values
    Given a row in patient_therapy_shipment with <column> as an invalid date
    When the enrichment process runs
    Then an error is raised: "Invalid date in column: <column>"
    And the row is not processed

    Examples:
      | column         |
      | ship_date      |
      | dob            |
      | first_ship_date|

  Scenario: Display enriched_patient_therapy_shipment result
    Given enrichment completes successfully for all valid rows
    When the output is generated
    Then the enriched_patient_therapy_shipment table is displayed with all source and derived columns

# END
